A||||40||87GTBro||Don't you wish you were buying a GT?||||6||
Z||000000||87GTBro||12-14-1999||09:00 PM||||Does anyone remember the FIRST day you bought your Fiero?  <BR>What were your thoughts and emotions about the car?<BR>Have they changed?<P>I am buying my first Fiero tomorrow morning.  '86.5 GT  I'll let you know how it was.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||09:42 PM||||Of course, I remember the day I brought my baby home (it was actually bought by my wife, in another state about 3 weeks earlier-long story)!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I almost cried.  I'd been waiting for one of these for 15 years.  My emotions *have* changed.  I feel a stronger attachment to my baby everytime I look at her (reaching for a Kleenex).  Congratulations on your new Fiero!!  If you feel anything like I do, this will be a Kodak moment.  BTW--really do bring a camera.  Have someone take some pics of you with your car before you even drive it.  You will cherish these.  Have I gone overboard?  Maybe I am a true Fieroholic!  Yee-haw!||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-14-1999||10:35 PM||||Yeah, what he said!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||12-15-1999||12:08 AM||||I liked my car more back when it was the innocent little Pontiac in the driveway. Now it's the little beast that doesn't run right becuase the owner(me) screwed something up and doesn't know what.<BR>Yeah, I still love it though. But it does need a good bath, too bad my driveway is on a hill or I'd push it out of the garage and wash it.<BR>I agree also, you will always cherrish the photos of you and the car before you even drive it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||12-15-1999||07:43 AM||||I had to wait a whole day after I bought mine so that they could inspect it and change the brakes. It was hard. Then My dad and I went to the car wash and made it look 1000000X better. The dealership never washed it! Good Luck With yours <P>1988 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000005||Clint||12-15-1999||07:53 AM||||all of mine have been an adventure.  many have come from great distances some from right around the corner.  If anyone wants to be bored i can eloborate.  I'm just hoping to get ahead financialy so i can start to do some customizing/detailing.  Painting etc..<P>such is life||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||07:58 AM||||Drove about 50 miles to check out an ad with little info.<BR> "87 GT, Good second car". <BR>Couldn't round up anyone to go with me.I expected it to be rough from the second car statment.<BR>When I pull up at the house it was Blue with spoiler and all accessories except leather and lumbar. Drove it and Bought it on the spot. could hardly sleep until I picked it up the next day. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||12-15-1999||09:07 AM||||Wolfhound, you lucky dog.  Wish I had a blue GT.<P>Remember in &lt;B&gt;The Godfather&lt;/B&gt; when Michael first sees Appolonia and says he's been hit by "the thunderbolt?"  That's how I felt each time I first saw a Fiero I would later own.||||reg||1
Z||000008||RossT||12-15-1999||10:08 AM||||I was like a little boy on Chistmas day. I had bought my car sight unseen over the phone. I know that can be dangerous, but I did not give a deposite.  The guy had the 88gt in storage with a cover over it.  As the cover was slowly being removed, like a christmas gift, I almost wet my pants! The more the cover came off, the bigger my smile got!!!!! Once the cover was off my very first reaction was: "this baby is mine!"||||reg||1
Z||000009||stsmithgt||12-15-1999||10:10 AM||||I wish I had a camera that fine sunny day!  I look outside at that beutiful white 86.5 fastback GT and ask,"Is that really mine?"  Oh yeah baby!  Have fun!||||reg||1
Z||000010||GT Bastard||12-15-1999||11:34 AM||||I first saw my '87 GT in a repairables lot at about 1am in the morning.  A friend of mine knew I had an interest in Fiero's, so he drove by the lot so I could take a look. The very next day, I took a look at the car in the lot and I loved it immediately.  Even with the front-end damage, it looked sweet as hell, and the interior was perfect. I've got it mostly finished now, but money is tight for this month, so it's gotta wait. Let us know how you like the car.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||12-15-1999||04:08 PM||||RossT--my smile wasn't the only thing that got bigger.  This is a sickness.  My name is Dave and I'm a Fieroholic.  I will change...(when I'm 6 ft. under! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
