Z||000013||theogre||12-15-1999||07:12 PM||||To answer the topic, No I don't.<P>Other than the V6. I don't like the GT much. My 87SC also has a trim kit on it that I've yet to see on another car. The trim is part of why I haven't painted it yet. I want to get the trim duplicated before I paint it, which is likely to force me to destroy it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Wolfhound||12-15-1999||08:22 PM||||Ogre, Trim kit? Are you talking about a applied vinyl trim. have a photo?<BR>Coy||||reg||5
Z||000015||Dave85||12-15-1999||09:23 PM||||Like RossT I bought my '85 GT over the phone. I found an ad from Oklahoma City(160 miles away) that said '85 GT needs work $900.  To make along story short the lady called and said she'd take $500 if I wanted to come and get it. I drove over and when I got there I couldn't believe it the car was is great shape. Interior is near perfect, could use a paint job, though not too bad.<BR>Can you say " Happy, Happy, Happy" ||||reg||1
Z||000016||four50four||12-15-1999||09:38 PM||||well, did you get it??||||reg||1
Z||000017||87GTBro||12-15-1999||11:16 PM||||	I got it!<BR>	A brand new (new to me) red 1986.5 Fiero GT Fastback is now sitting out in my driveway begging me to get it running properly.  Buying this car was not as exciting as I thought it should have been.  I was saddened to see the condition the car was in.  It had been sitting in the parking lot of an auto shop for years.  Driving it home felt like adopting a dog or cat from the animal shelter.  We had to charge up it's poor little battery and clean its spark plugs.  We even had to spray starter fluid in it's mouth to get it to start.  The poor thing was dull, it's skin covered with dust and dirt.  But, now I am happy that it is finally home where it belongs.  I am sure after I get his engine all cleaned up, he will be a happier Fiero too.  As soon as I got off of work this afternoon I went to work.  I gave it a bath.  Something I'm sure it hasn't had in about 2 years.  And I polished it and waxed it and now I can see myself in it.  <BR>	I am absolutely positive that after I get it running like a champ, I will be a lot more satisfied and feel that the $1750 didn't go to waiste.<BR>	One thing that I am worried about is that it doesn't have a clear title.  The owner didn't have the original.  He said the car is paid for, but the bank that it was financed through never sent him the original when he paid it off.  I do have the duplicate though.  Maybe I can file for a lost title.  I hope that works.||||reg||1
Z||000018||batboy||12-15-1999||11:21 PM||||I've bought vehicles before with duplicate titles and never had a problem. As long as the duplicate title is valid, you'll be ok.||||reg||1
Z||000019||ChadMan||12-16-1999||09:26 AM||||My wife thinks I'm crazy, but if my ship ever comes in, I plan to assemble the following collection, which I think exemplifies the best of every year:<P>An 84 Indy Fiero.<BR>An 85 SE V6 (without aero bodywork).<BR>An 86 SE V6 (with aero bodywork).<BR>An 87 GT, preferably in blue.<BR>An 88 Formula, preferably with T-tops.<P>And the entire collection would cost considerably less than a luxury SUV.||||reg||7
Z||000020||bHooper||12-16-1999||10:18 AM||||i remember that day 10 years ago well... i picked the car up winston and was driving it back to greensboro (about 30 miles) when i decided to stop and get gas.  that was when i  realized that i didn't know where the fuel door release was   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  i couldn't reach my friend to ask him... so i just pushed the envelope of fuel mileage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  that nite, my buddy (in his identical 86.5 gt) and i raced back home.  now until this car, i had been driving a CRX with a tall gear ratio, but on that 80 mph drive through the city i must have hit the rev limiter 6 times (shutting the engine down every one)!  needless to say, that NEVER happened again.  now each day, i look into my garage and see that same car, on jack stands, w/o a body or a tranny, and i still dream of whacking the rev limiter!  one day... one day!<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 12-16-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000021||william_thorniii||12-16-1999||06:55 PM||||On a similar topic, last summer I let a roomate borrow my 87 SC for a weekend trip from Flint, MI to Spartanburg, SC since it gets considerably better gas mileage than does his 93 Silverado.  I never thought to tell him where the fuel door release was, a couple of years ago he worked as a tech at a GM dealer.  This is the guy that I always go to with my questions... so he is very experienced with automotive mechanics.  When he got back he told me that on the way down he looked for it for about half of an hour including many unreasonable places such as under the front and rear compartment lids.  Luckily he wasn't too far from town so he got back in with the intention of heading back to ask me.  While fastening his belt, he caught the release with the corner of his eye. ||||reg||1
Z||000022||jhogans||12-16-1999||07:00 PM||||I don't feel bad now.  I didn't know where the release was either.  I was at an oil change place getting my fuel system cleaned and the guy asked me to pop the gas but I couldn't because I didn't know where the lever was.  We looked all over the place for about 10 minutes and still couldn't find it.  do I told him that's ok.  I will do it another time.  As I was putting my seatbelt on, I saw the lever.  I was too embarrassed to tell the guy I found it, so I just went home.||||reg||10
Z||000023||turbo86se||12-16-1999||10:35 PM||||My first Fiero was a 85 coupe. No options, except air and spoiler. I loved it! It needed lots of work, clutch,brakes,suspension,gaskets... but it ran great. I bought it on the spot. The next day I picked it up with my girlfriend. The first stop was the gas station. I shouldn't say this, but I looked everywhere for the gas lever! After a few minutes, my g'friend walked up to me in the car and asked what was wrong. I said "how in the h$!! do you put gas in this thing?" She just looked at me and laughed, after a another minute or two, I found it! I was so relieved! I've been hooked ever since!   My name is Joel, and I'm a Fieroholic!  LOL||||reg||1
Z||000024||87GTBro||12-16-1999||11:29 PM||||I am starting to like my little baby more every day.  Today, I changed the oil, filter, air filter, fuel filter and spark plugs and now it purrs like a kitten.<BR>Actually more like a lion.  A small little hole about the size of a quarter in my exhaust pipe about 2 inches from the back side of the cat makes this little car sound BIG.<BR>I kinda like it but I'd better get it fixed.<P>Now I only have one problem!!  I CAN'T DRIVE IT!!!  I have to wait for the insurance agent to get the policy started, then I have to get it registered and inspected.  <BR>GRRRRR...||||reg||10
