Z||000037||sdm1964||01-20-2000||07:13 AM||||First things first,<BR>Monkey-I know how you feel, my wife bought mine for me too. I found it in the paper but had to go out of town, in the national guard. I was coming back from atlanta, I really was hauling a** back from atlanta to get home to drive my new toy. I was not really paying attention and ran out of gas on a back road. I had to walk 2 miles in the rain to the gas station. <P>Ross, nice car, does it have the grey interior? Looks like my 85GT only with the aeroback. I want to get those rims for mine.<P>Ps. I knew where my gas level was because i worked at a pontiac dealer when they first came out.||||reg||14
Z||000038||RossT||01-20-2000||07:17 AM||||Grey-cloth||||reg||1
Z||000039||AL||01-20-2000||09:13 PM||||WELL THIS IS MY STORY, i bought my 86GT for 900, the whol car was perfect except it had a break lens broken, but every thing else was fine. i had to drive 80 miles to get it, well i started to drive it home when i notice that thE car is running hot, i think to myself keep going cause you are to far from home, well i finnaly pulled in a gas station and the radiator was shot. when i tried to start it up, it didn't want to start, well i towed it home and took the heads ofF (head gasket blown), well i took the heads off sent them out, while the heads were getting redone i did the radiator. i finnaly got every thing back and put it all together, i changed the wires spark plugs vac lines tranny service and finnaly lubed it all. then i cleaned the fuel injction and tires, all for the grand price of 1.400 and my baby works great.i would send a pic but i'm on web tv and i don't think i could send one with this system. long live the fiero,AL. ||||reg||1
Z||000040||stimpy||01-20-2000||11:40 PM||||Well, everyone has a story and this is mine.  I always loved the looks of the Fiero but had long resigned myself to never owning one. I am stature enhanced (6'6") and had tried sitting in a classmates graduation present, a brand new 85 coupe, no sunroof.  Not a fit. Fast forward 12 years, my dad decides to catch the fiero bug, trading his 90 lebaron convertible pretty much straight across for a bright red and silver 86 GT with a sunroof. Lo and behold, I actually fit! I was in lust. I would spend hours detailing that beautiful car, even waxing the wheel wells and spare tire compartment.(really!)  My dad is a hell of a role model when it comes to Fiero insanity (hi dad!) first trying to have his 2.8 magically bored out to 3.4 (don't believe the hype) then putting in the monster 3.8 sc. (what a motor!) <BR>So it was predictable that when I sold my present car that he would suggest a fiero.  Looked in the Auto trader and saw 2 that had my interest, a blue 88 coupe with t-tops in Sacramento, and a Gold 86 GT with sunroof in Stockton. My pick, $2500. Well, one test drive in the GT and I never mades it to Sacramento. And I stillmake every excuse to take he long way home one year and one motor later.    ||||reg||1
